## Expected Editors and Limits

- All expected values are LaTeX, not code-style sqrt()/abs() or display prose.
  Numeric values are legitimate scalar real answers; radical numeric values
  need the math-capable editor/full keyboard, not plain decimal-only entry.
  Existing fallback maps numeric to number and exact to math; no interaction
  artifact was read or authored, so this is not an actual widget approval.
- Chinese yes/no and position keys are `\text{...}`; infinity, empty set and
  intervals are formula-editor exact representations. These are plausible
  input targets, but parsing and normalized string equality are NOT evidence
  of successful real editor entry/edit/reserialization.
- Actual MathLive setter-plus-keyboard-edit tests were NOT run, as browsers and
  finalize are explicitly unauthorized. All 33 exact keys retain that pending
  requirement; no test attempt, focus retry or successful editing result is
  invented. A later authorized stage must prove the real input contract.
- Parameter interval endpoints and sign/domain branches are complete. Interval
  labels specify the canonical format, avoiding an assumed general logical
  equivalence test for inequalities.
- Proof/open construction and drawing answers 140,141,142,145-148 correctly
  have concrete displays and empty auto parts. 151 must join that group.
- No physical units, names, dates or historical entities were added to these
  coordinate/algebra answers.

